WEBVTT

00:45.791 --> 00:47.583
My name is David Burroughs.

00:48.333 --> 00:52.291
I'm currently serving the fifth year of
a life sentence for killing my little boy.

00:53.791 --> 00:56.333
The thing is, I didn't do it.

00:57.041 --> 00:58.957
Not that I'm innocent.

00:58.958 --> 01:01.833
A father's job
is to protect his child from harm.

01:02.416 --> 01:03.250
I failed.

01:04.958 --> 01:08.125
Matthew was murdered in his bedroom
as I slept down the hall.

01:08.791 --> 01:10.290
Knowing he died alone,

01:10.291 --> 01:12.458
wondering why his father
never came to save him.

01:14.041 --> 01:15.833
That's my real life sentence.

01:18.333 --> 01:19.915
I happen to be serving it here,

01:19.916 --> 01:23.041
in the protective custody unit
at Briggs Penitentiary.

01:24.041 --> 01:26.666
Prison is designed
to strip away your identity.

01:27.458 --> 01:29.166
Your sense of self.

01:30.583 --> 01:32.708
The man I was no longer exists.

01:33.333 --> 01:37.083
It's why I've refused
to see any visitors since arriving.

01:38.041 --> 01:39.125
Not even family.

01:40.708 --> 01:42.250
Especially family.

01:43.375 --> 01:44.833
I know what they think.

01:45.750 --> 01:49.750
With the evidence against me,
what they had no choice but to think.

01:50.250 --> 01:53.625
I don't blame them,
but I don't want to see them either.

01:54.625 --> 01:56.666
It's better for everyone to forget.

01:57.291 --> 01:59.208
Because the past never changes.

02:00.666 --> 02:03.166
Until one day, it does.

02:16.083 --> 02:17.708
Open number nine!

02:20.791 --> 02:22.125
Let's go, Burroughs.

02:22.791 --> 02:24.082
What's going on?

02:24.083 --> 02:25.166
You have a visitor.

02:25.666 --> 02:27.791
Your sister-in-law, Rachel Mills.

02:28.375 --> 02:31.207
- That can't be right.
- And yet here we are.

02:31.208 --> 02:34.040
Why anyone would visit
a child killer is beyond me.

02:34.041 --> 02:36.333
But I've learned
to just roll with the crazy shit.

02:36.916 --> 02:38.791
Let's go. Up.

02:40.125 --> 02:41.458
If I refuse?

02:42.541 --> 02:44.708
Oh, Burroughs, please do.

03:20.375 --> 03:23.540
- What are you doing here, Rachel?
- You look different.

03:23.541 --> 03:25.375
Yeah, well, it's been five years.

03:27.666 --> 03:28.500
Are you okay?

03:30.541 --> 03:32.333
Sorry, stupid question.

03:36.875 --> 03:38.790
Did something happen to Cheryl?

03:38.791 --> 03:39.791
No.

03:40.541 --> 03:42.707
No, no, she's fine. She's actually great.

03:42.708 --> 03:43.957
Okay.

03:43.958 --> 03:45.083
I mean, she's…

03:50.500 --> 03:51.708
She doesn't know I'm here.

03:53.041 --> 03:55.708
- Why are you here?
- I need to show you something.

03:56.291 --> 03:59.958
And just before I do,
I know it's gonna sound crazy.

04:01.041 --> 04:04.832
I have this friend from college, Irene.
She's married, two kids, the whole thing.

04:04.833 --> 04:06.207
A couple weeks ago,

04:06.208 --> 04:09.166
she posted photos online of a trip
they took to Six Flags in Springfield.

04:10.333 --> 04:11.708
Including this one.

04:16.125 --> 04:19.790
Crazy. You come down here to show me
a picture of your friend and her kids?

04:19.791 --> 04:20.958
Look closer, David.

04:26.583 --> 04:27.916
Tell me what you see.

04:39.958 --> 04:40.958
He…

04:42.708 --> 04:44.124
He-He…

04:44.125 --> 04:46.208
- He looks like Matthew.
- I know.

04:47.166 --> 04:50.166
- The birthmark's smaller.
- Doctor said it'd shrink as he got older.

04:51.458 --> 04:53.125
Only he never got older.

04:54.000 --> 04:55.500
Which means that this is…

04:57.083 --> 05:00.457
just a photo of a little boy that looks
like Matthew, if he was still alive.

05:00.458 --> 05:01.291
Right?

05:03.041 --> 05:04.249
Did you show Cheryl?

05:04.250 --> 05:06.791
No. It took her a long time
to rebuild her life.

05:07.625 --> 05:11.499
I'm not gonna blow it up
over something that… can't be true.

05:11.500 --> 05:15.958
- You wouldn't come if you didn't think--
- That Matthew's somehow still alive? Yeah.

05:16.708 --> 05:18.165
And I know how insane that sounds.

05:18.166 --> 05:20.625
Just as insane as people thinking
that I killed him in the first place.

05:21.208 --> 05:22.666
Well, I never did.

05:24.291 --> 05:25.791
I found him.

05:27.375 --> 05:28.790
He was dead.

05:28.791 --> 05:29.707
I know.

05:29.708 --> 05:31.582
But if there's a chance,

05:31.583 --> 05:35.666
no matter how impossible,
that he is somehow still alive…

05:36.791 --> 05:38.707
Time's up, Burroughs!

05:38.708 --> 05:40.749
You-You need to turn the phone back on.

05:40.750 --> 05:42.040
You need to turn it back on.

05:42.041 --> 05:44.250
I don't need to do anything.
Come on, let's go.

05:45.541 --> 05:47.290
- Come on.
- Show Cheryl.

05:47.291 --> 05:48.500
Come on. Up!

05:49.041 --> 05:50.541
Show Cheryl.

05:52.083 --> 05:52.916
Let's go.

06:11.083 --> 06:13.540
- I need to see the warden.
- Again with the needs.

06:13.541 --> 06:16.790
You're making a lot of demands today,
Burroughs. I'd be careful.

06:16.791 --> 06:18.541
Come on, let me tell him--

06:19.375 --> 06:21.165
Can't say I didn't warn you.

06:21.166 --> 06:23.166
Come on. Get him up.

06:26.625 --> 06:27.999
Please.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.208
Just talk to him.

06:32.875 --> 06:35.707
Just let me talk to him. Please.

06:35.708 --> 06:38.000
Oh, yeah, I'll get right on that.

06:41.958 --> 06:43.041
Son of a bitch.

07:21.750 --> 07:23.250
Tell me what you see.

07:27.583 --> 07:28.875
Look closer, David.

07:42.291 --> 07:43.333
Dad.

07:46.250 --> 07:47.416
Wake up, Burroughs.

07:49.291 --> 07:50.708
Warden wants to see you.

07:52.541 --> 07:54.582
Officer Wesson
filed a disciplinary report.

07:54.583 --> 07:55.500
You wanna tell me what happened?

07:57.250 --> 07:58.582
I asked to see you.

07:58.583 --> 08:01.458
Doesn't sound like the kinda thing
that gets you thrown into solitary.

08:02.041 --> 08:03.874
Might have asked more than once.

08:03.875 --> 08:04.833
Hmm.

08:06.375 --> 08:08.624
Does this have something to do
with Rachel Mills visiting yesterday?

08:08.625 --> 08:10.291
I mean, it's been five years.
What brought her out?

08:11.208 --> 08:15.082
She showed me a photo of a young boy
taken at Six Flags a few weeks ago.

08:15.083 --> 08:16.708
And he looked like Matthew.

08:17.416 --> 08:18.833
Like what he would look like now.

08:19.416 --> 08:20.874
I mean exactly like Matthew.

08:20.875 --> 08:23.791
Like, down to the--
The birthmark on his cheek.

08:24.833 --> 08:28.332
- I thought if you saw the photo--
- I don't need to see the photo, David.

08:28.333 --> 08:29.582
I get it.

08:29.583 --> 08:33.999
Do you think you're the first lifer
to grab on to some impossible idea

08:34.000 --> 08:35.790
that this has all been some big mistake?

08:35.791 --> 08:38.165
You're like a son to me, David.

08:38.166 --> 08:39.999
I was at your trial.

08:40.000 --> 08:42.083
The DNA was a match to Matthew.

08:43.583 --> 08:45.916
- What about Rachel?
- What about her?

08:47.833 --> 08:50.624
She's a respected journalist.
Maybe she's onto something.

08:50.625 --> 08:52.332
She was a respected journalist.

08:52.333 --> 08:54.957
She got fired from the Globe
a few years ago.

08:54.958 --> 08:56.332
What happened?

08:56.333 --> 08:57.916
I don't know the details.

08:59.791 --> 09:03.040
She's Cheryl's sister.
She's-- She's not gonna drag up the past.

09:03.041 --> 09:04.832
Well, Rachel's not my concern. You are.

09:04.833 --> 09:07.082
You think it's a coincidence
you ended up in my prison?

09:07.083 --> 09:08.999
I pulled strings to get you here,

09:09.000 --> 09:11.332
and I promised your old man
I'd look out for you.

09:11.333 --> 09:12.541
Then help me.

09:13.541 --> 09:16.165
Look, you've got friends in the BPD.
You could ask them for the murder book.

09:16.166 --> 09:17.540
- You can't be serious.
- Listen to me.

09:17.541 --> 09:19.540
In five years,
I've never asked you for anything.

09:19.541 --> 09:22.290
And you never had to.
I care about you, David.

09:22.291 --> 09:25.665
The moment you think there's a way out,
this place breaks you.

09:25.666 --> 09:29.125
It's not about getting out. It's just that
I know something no one else does.

09:30.541 --> 09:31.541
What?

09:33.208 --> 09:34.625
That I'm innocent.

09:39.541 --> 09:41.333
Someone else was there that night.

09:44.500 --> 09:45.375
Prisoner's ready.

09:54.000 --> 09:55.000
Matthew's dead, David.

09:56.958 --> 09:58.833
No photograph's gonna change that.

10:08.375 --> 10:10.791
Stella, can you come in here, please?

10:11.791 --> 10:13.624
Can you clear my schedule for today?

10:13.625 --> 10:16.000
Yes, sir. Anything else?

10:16.958 --> 10:18.916
Yeah, book me
on the next flight to Boston.

10:44.541 --> 10:45.708
Hey, Soph.

10:46.666 --> 10:47.500
Hey.

10:48.291 --> 10:50.207
- Good to see you, Adam.
- How are you?

10:50.208 --> 10:52.249
- Good, how are you?
- Yeah, good.

10:52.250 --> 10:54.416
Wow, look what the cat dragged in.

10:55.125 --> 10:57.000
Hey, Sophie.

10:58.666 --> 10:59.790
You're looking well.

10:59.791 --> 11:02.249
Always a charmer. Why didn't you call?

11:02.250 --> 11:03.999
Oh, yeah. That's a good question.

11:04.000 --> 11:06.499
Can't a guy visit his friend
without having some secret agenda?

11:06.500 --> 11:08.625
Yeah, he can. But you have one, Dad.

11:09.875 --> 11:12.040
It was a last minute-thing.
How's he doing?

11:12.041 --> 11:13.540
Well, you know my brother.

11:13.541 --> 11:16.166
He's more worried about the Sox
making the playoffs than he is the cancer.

11:17.041 --> 11:19.082
Um, where's Lenny at?

11:19.083 --> 11:21.040
- In the living room.
- Okay.

11:21.041 --> 11:23.500
- Uh, give me a minute?
- Yeah.

11:26.208 --> 11:27.874
Don't ask me.

11:27.875 --> 11:30.166
Two on and nobody out.

11:30.916 --> 11:31.874
Another base hit…

11:31.875 --> 11:35.416
I wish I could sit around and watch
the game in the middle of the day.

11:37.708 --> 11:39.916
Not with how these clowns are playing.

11:43.541 --> 11:47.166
Adam's outside with Sophie.
Hope you don't mind we dropped by.

11:49.083 --> 11:50.333
Guess it depends on why.

11:50.916 --> 11:52.875
Mm, I was in the neighborhood.

11:54.000 --> 11:57.666
Last time I checked,
Briggs was in Maine, not Boston.

11:58.916 --> 11:59.875
David came to see me.

12:02.083 --> 12:05.540
He, uh… He wants a copy
of Matthew's murder book.

12:05.541 --> 12:06.541
Why?

12:07.666 --> 12:09.458
It's been five years. Why ask for it now?

12:10.916 --> 12:12.625
He always said he was innocent.

12:14.166 --> 12:16.249
I think a part of him even believes it.

12:16.250 --> 12:18.708
He's my son. I want to believe it.

12:19.291 --> 12:20.708
But we both know better.

12:24.291 --> 12:25.458
What?

12:26.250 --> 12:31.707
I've come across
every kind of killer imaginable at Briggs.

12:31.708 --> 12:35.749
You know, plenty claim they're innocent.
Most claim they've changed.

12:35.750 --> 12:39.040
But Lenny, there's something in their eyes
when they talk to you.

12:39.041 --> 12:43.415
Something that can't be erased
with time or meds or religion.

12:43.416 --> 12:44.541
It's like a…

12:45.708 --> 12:48.665
It's like a snake, you know, under a rock.

12:48.666 --> 12:50.041
It's always there.

12:51.875 --> 12:54.125
- But with David--
- So now you believe him?

13:00.125 --> 13:01.375
Maybe I'm just getting old.

13:04.125 --> 13:06.790
You sure there's nothing in that file
that can come back on us?

13:06.791 --> 13:07.875
How could it?

13:09.291 --> 13:12.041
Nothing we did that night
changed a damn thing.

13:15.916 --> 13:17.582
Hey, Pops, what's going on?

13:17.583 --> 13:19.415
It's probably better that you don't know.

13:19.416 --> 13:22.500
Yeah, I'm sure you're right,
but why don't you tell me anyways?

13:25.333 --> 13:27.541
Rachel Mills came
to visit David yesterday.

13:32.750 --> 13:33.833
Rachel?

13:34.583 --> 13:35.416
About what?

13:37.791 --> 13:38.625
Matthew.

13:39.208 --> 13:41.291
David thinks he's still alive.

14:10.291 --> 14:11.416
Hey, Burroughs.

14:21.708 --> 14:23.500
Warden Mackenzie says
to make sure it stays hidden.

14:31.458 --> 14:34.624
No signs of forced entry.
No fingerprints or foreign DNA.

14:34.625 --> 14:37.915
Even the defendant admits
he was asleep alone inside the house.

14:37.916 --> 14:40.624
He claimed he woke up
and discovered the body.

14:40.625 --> 14:43.665
Mr. Burroughs has a history
of night terrors.

14:43.666 --> 14:45.957
And during a night terror,

14:45.958 --> 14:48.790
is it possible for someone
to inflict harm on another person

14:48.791 --> 14:52.707
without being conscious of it
or even remembering it when they wake up?

14:52.708 --> 14:54.666
Yes. It is.

14:55.250 --> 14:57.082
Due to the severity of the injuries,

14:57.083 --> 14:58.457
a visual ID was impossible.

14:58.458 --> 15:01.665
But DNA tests confirmed
the body was Matthew Burroughs.

15:01.666 --> 15:04.290
And would these injuries be consistent

15:04.291 --> 15:06.999
with the baseball bat found in the woods?

15:07.000 --> 15:07.875
Yes.

15:08.500 --> 15:09.541
They would.

15:10.541 --> 15:12.457
Let's talk about what happened next.

15:12.458 --> 15:14.749
You're neighbors
with the defendant, correct?

15:14.750 --> 15:15.707
Yes.

15:15.708 --> 15:18.707
Can you tell us what you saw
the night of the murder, Mrs. Winslow?

15:18.708 --> 15:21.957
I saw a man bury something
in the woods behind his home.

15:21.958 --> 15:25.915
And is the man that you saw
that night in this courtroom today?

15:25.916 --> 15:27.916
Yes, it was David Burroughs.

15:48.208 --> 15:51.125
Jumping up and down the floor

15:52.208 --> 15:55.916
My head is an animal…

15:57.500 --> 16:02.791
So, I'm still waiting
on three RSVPs for the baby shower.

16:04.625 --> 16:06.625
Hello? Earth to Rachel?

16:08.000 --> 16:10.041
Yeah, e-vite reminder, I'm on it.

16:11.541 --> 16:12.833
What's going on?

16:13.458 --> 16:15.790
You seem more Rachel than normal.

16:15.791 --> 16:17.790
Why, thank you.

16:17.791 --> 16:20.332
- Didn't you have an interview last week?
- Yeah.

16:20.333 --> 16:22.499
- Uh, the Pawtucket Times.
- Hmm.

16:22.500 --> 16:23.957
They're keeping my résumé on file,

16:23.958 --> 16:26.458
which is code for we know who you are
and what happened.

16:27.041 --> 16:28.457
I'm sorry.

16:28.458 --> 16:30.499
But what? I hear a "but" coming.

16:30.500 --> 16:34.291
Well, you've interviewed
at every paper in the New England area.

16:34.791 --> 16:36.290
Maybe it's time to move on?

16:36.291 --> 16:39.291
You mean teach Intro to Journalism
at Quincy College for the rest of my life?

16:40.583 --> 16:43.166
Just thought if enough time
had passed, you know.

16:44.333 --> 16:45.916
You'd find your way back?

16:47.541 --> 16:48.457
Yeah.

16:48.458 --> 16:51.124
You can't let what happened
at the Globe define you.

16:51.125 --> 16:54.416
- Why not? Everyone else has.
- No, you're a great journalist.

16:55.000 --> 16:56.083
Okay? You just…

16:56.791 --> 16:58.958
You need to get out there
and find a story.

17:12.208 --> 17:14.708
So there's something
I wanted to talk to you about.

17:15.958 --> 17:17.333
- Oh.
- Ooh!

17:17.916 --> 17:20.707
- You okay?
- Oh, yeah. Sorry.

17:20.708 --> 17:23.124
Yeah, no, I'm fine, I'm fine, I'm fine.

17:23.125 --> 17:24.083
I just…

17:24.583 --> 17:26.833
She's really moving around today.

17:28.333 --> 17:30.000
She?

17:31.666 --> 17:33.125
You found out?

17:33.625 --> 17:36.415
I thought the Ronster wanted
to do some sort of gender reveal party.

17:36.416 --> 17:38.207
You know I love it when you call him that.

17:38.208 --> 17:39.083
Oh, you do?

17:39.666 --> 17:40.583
Wow.

17:41.375 --> 17:43.458
A nurse at our last ultrasound
let it slip.

17:44.083 --> 17:45.083
Hi.

17:46.291 --> 17:48.166
How's it feel having a little girl?

17:48.791 --> 17:49.750
Um…

17:50.458 --> 17:52.375
Yeah, uh, it feels…

17:54.166 --> 17:55.250
right.

17:59.666 --> 18:01.541
Like I'm not replacing him.

18:02.666 --> 18:04.333
I know that must sound silly.

18:05.291 --> 18:06.291
It doesn't.

18:07.375 --> 18:08.333
Not even a little.

18:10.958 --> 18:11.958
It's okay.

18:14.375 --> 18:16.749
Uh, I'm fine. It's just hormones.

18:16.750 --> 18:19.750
- Um, can you get me some tissues?
- Of course.

18:25.083 --> 18:27.083
Oh, um, what did you want
to talk to me about?

18:28.375 --> 18:31.250
Uh, nothing. Not important.

18:48.583 --> 18:50.874
Journalism isn't just
about reporting the news.

18:50.875 --> 18:54.374
It's about seeking the truth.
Holding power to account.

18:54.375 --> 18:56.290
Giving a voice to those
who don't have one,

18:56.291 --> 18:58.624
but listening to them
deeply and respectfully.

18:58.625 --> 19:01.499
That's what a journalist
should be trying to do.

19:01.500 --> 19:02.540
Okay.

19:02.541 --> 19:04.832
Next week,
we'll be discussing media literacy,

19:04.833 --> 19:07.749
and I want everyone to bring in
an article that contains examples

19:07.750 --> 19:09.415
of attribution and sourcing.

19:09.416 --> 19:11.958
And no, Jordy, it cannot be digital, okay?

19:17.583 --> 19:18.540
Hello?

19:18.541 --> 19:21.915
This is a collect call
from an inmate at Briggs Penitentiary.

19:21.916 --> 19:24.583
If you'd like to accept
these charges, press 1.

19:25.791 --> 19:27.707
- Hello?
- Rachel, it's David.

19:27.708 --> 19:30.499
Don't know how much time I've got,
but I talked to Mackenzie.

19:30.500 --> 19:33.499
I have some new information.
Can you please come back here?

19:33.500 --> 19:35.958
Yeah. Drive up
first thing tomorrow morning.

19:37.458 --> 19:38.874
- Okay.
- I'll see you then.

19:38.875 --> 19:39.791
Okay.

20:24.958 --> 20:26.250
David Burroughs.

20:27.000 --> 20:28.625
Ross Sumner. It's a pleasure to meet you.

20:30.458 --> 20:33.291
Do you know you're the only
college graduate in the PCU?

20:33.875 --> 20:37.375
Not to mention law professor at BU.
It's very impressive.

20:38.416 --> 20:42.291
I have been starved
for some intelligent conversation.

20:43.583 --> 20:46.666
You did your undergrad at Amherst, right?

20:48.791 --> 20:50.957
- Want to know where I went?
- Not really.

20:50.958 --> 20:52.583
I went to Williams College.

20:53.250 --> 20:56.957
Yeah, we are both graduates
of the Small Ivies.

20:56.958 --> 20:58.875
Jesus, is that Ross Sumner?

20:59.750 --> 21:01.250
Yeah, I guess so. Why?

21:02.083 --> 21:03.249
Why?

21:03.250 --> 21:05.957
They found six bodies stuffed
in a sub-zero on his family's estate

21:05.958 --> 21:08.249
and two more
in his Upper West Side penthouse.

21:08.250 --> 21:09.750
He's insane. How'd he get work detail?

21:11.125 --> 21:12.500
It's above my pay grade.

21:14.625 --> 21:18.708
You, uh, had your first visitor
the other day, isn't that right?

21:19.458 --> 21:22.541
Your sister-in-law, Rachel Mills.

21:23.208 --> 21:26.291
- How'd you know that?
- I know all about you, David.

21:27.416 --> 21:30.666
And I find you fascinating.

21:32.208 --> 21:35.708
See, I killed 11 people.

21:36.750 --> 21:41.082
And they were all strangers to me.
It just meant nothing, props on the stage.

21:41.083 --> 21:45.583
But you, David, you killed your own son.

21:46.458 --> 21:48.500
The flesh of your flesh.

21:50.208 --> 21:52.208
So tell me, David,

21:53.708 --> 21:56.499
when you brought that bat down

21:56.500 --> 21:58.458
on his little skull…

22:00.458 --> 22:02.083
what did that feel like?

22:05.458 --> 22:07.250
I think you should back off.

22:11.125 --> 22:12.250
Okay.

22:14.750 --> 22:15.833
Okay.

22:16.708 --> 22:18.708
I'm just making conversation here.

22:35.250 --> 22:36.166
Fight!

22:44.458 --> 22:47.208
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
Let them tire themselves out for a second.

22:47.791 --> 22:49.291
Yeah! Fuck him up!

22:53.291 --> 22:56.416
That's right. Nobody's coming to save you.

23:14.541 --> 23:15.874
Dad.

23:15.875 --> 23:17.041
Wake up.

23:18.708 --> 23:19.791
Wake up.

23:31.666 --> 23:32.875
Fuck you!

23:34.125 --> 23:37.249
Get up! Get up! Get him up! Get up!

23:37.250 --> 23:38.666
Get up! Get up!

23:39.458 --> 23:41.415
All right, all right. All right!

23:41.416 --> 23:43.291
Hey, it's done! You're done!

23:53.250 --> 23:54.416
I saw what you did.

23:56.041 --> 23:57.833
I don't know what you're talking about.

24:09.291 --> 24:11.165
Ross Sumner's housed in permanent Ad Seg.

24:11.166 --> 24:12.832
How the hell does he get
on a PCU work detail?

24:12.833 --> 24:15.125
Looks like some kind
of clerical mix-up during a transfer.

24:16.083 --> 24:18.665
Want to explain why you and Officer Lu
just stood there?

24:18.666 --> 24:21.832
An altercation broke out between
two dangerous and violent inmates.

24:21.833 --> 24:23.749
You mean a cannibalistic
psychopath jumped--

24:23.750 --> 24:25.458
A man who beat his own son to death.

24:26.208 --> 24:29.832
With all due respect, Warden,
we were working a 50-man detail.

24:29.833 --> 24:32.457
We engaged when we had to
and when I felt it was safe to do so,

24:32.458 --> 24:34.791
and I'm not gonna apologize for that.

24:39.416 --> 24:41.958
- All right. That'll be all.
- Sir.

24:57.833 --> 25:00.041
Rachel Mills.
I'm here to see David Burroughs.

25:17.416 --> 25:18.665
Jesus, what happened?

25:18.666 --> 25:20.249
I got attacked.

25:20.250 --> 25:22.125
- You okay?
- I'm fine.

25:22.958 --> 25:24.041
Don't worry about it.

25:27.208 --> 25:28.625
What did Mackenzie say?

25:29.958 --> 25:33.416
He said I was a lifer grasping at straws,
looking for a way out.

25:34.041 --> 25:37.083
But he also said
that you were fired from the Globe.

25:38.958 --> 25:41.999
Yeah. I teach at Quincy College now.

25:42.000 --> 25:42.958
You sound thrilled.

25:43.541 --> 25:45.457
I loved being a reporter, so, yeah.

25:45.458 --> 25:46.666
It's been hard.

25:48.333 --> 25:49.666
Is that what this is?

25:51.250 --> 25:52.583
It's just a story for you?

25:53.375 --> 25:54.708
- No.
- You sure?

25:55.291 --> 25:57.250
- David, no.
- Then what is it?

26:05.291 --> 26:08.791
The worst things that happen in life
usually can't be fixed.

26:11.916 --> 26:15.791
No matter how much we wish they could,
we can't go back and make things right.

26:17.916 --> 26:20.250
But if Matthew's alive and we find him,

26:21.250 --> 26:23.458
then maybe this is one time we can.

26:26.541 --> 26:27.916
That's why I'm here.

26:29.083 --> 26:31.625
Mackenzie gave me Matthew's case file.

26:32.375 --> 26:34.250
Are you sure you want to do this?

26:35.833 --> 26:36.833
Well,

26:37.958 --> 26:40.500
I'm getting a free continental breakfast
at the Briggs Motor Lodge.

26:41.250 --> 26:43.500
And, you know,
I'm a sucker for a day-old bagel, so…

26:45.416 --> 26:48.332
- I'm in. What am I looking for?
- It's not what, it's who.

26:48.333 --> 26:51.790
'Cause if Matthew wasn't the little boy
I found that night, who was he?

26:51.791 --> 26:53.832
We'd be looking for a Caucasian boy

26:53.833 --> 26:57.332
the same age and size as Matthew
who went missing before the murder.

26:57.333 --> 26:59.749
The National Center for Missing
and Exploited Children

26:59.750 --> 27:01.499
has the best database. I'll look there.

27:01.500 --> 27:03.707
What about the M.E.
who confirmed the body?

27:03.708 --> 27:05.707
Right, well, technically,
the DNA was a match,

27:05.708 --> 27:08.290
but it could have been altered in the lab.

27:08.291 --> 27:12.207
A visual ID wasn't possible due to
the nature of the injuries. Jesus Christ.

27:12.208 --> 27:15.082
- Yeah, it was probably the point.
- Why such extreme measures?

27:15.083 --> 27:17.040
Why not just take Matthew in the park?

27:17.041 --> 27:19.499
They knew I'd never stop looking.
No parent would.

27:19.500 --> 27:22.333
But if you thought he was dead
and were locked away for murder…

27:23.125 --> 27:24.875
But why you? Why Matthew?

27:25.625 --> 27:27.958
Okay, focus on questions
that can be answered.

27:28.541 --> 27:29.458
Like what?

27:32.541 --> 27:33.916
Hilde Winslow.

27:34.916 --> 27:35.957
Why did she lie?

27:35.958 --> 27:38.040
If she had nothing
to gain from your conviction,

27:38.041 --> 27:40.165
the most obvious answer
is that someone put her up to it.

27:40.166 --> 27:42.624
- Yeah.
- Maybe even the person that took Matthew.

27:42.625 --> 27:44.582
Well, start there.

27:44.583 --> 27:46.375
You got someone that can look into her?

27:48.541 --> 27:50.249
My old editor at the Globe.

27:50.250 --> 27:51.333
Rachel,

27:52.916 --> 27:54.541
if we're right about this…

27:56.750 --> 27:59.625
then there's someone
very dangerous behind it.

28:00.875 --> 28:02.666
So be careful.

28:05.958 --> 28:06.958
You too.

28:09.958 --> 28:13.082
You've reached the voicemail
of Jim Doherty with the Boston Globe.

28:13.083 --> 28:14.249
Please leave a message.

28:14.250 --> 28:16.915
Hey, Jim. Uh, it's Rachel.

28:16.916 --> 28:18.207
Hi.

28:18.208 --> 28:21.540
I know it's been a while,
um, but I need a favor.

28:21.541 --> 28:23.290
Could you run a name for me?

28:23.291 --> 28:26.458
Uh, it's a Hilde Winslow
from Revere, Mass.

28:27.041 --> 28:29.250
Thanks in advance. Talk to you soon.

28:40.250 --> 28:41.582
Hey.

28:41.583 --> 28:44.499
Did you, uh--
Did you see I sent the e-vite reminder?

28:44.500 --> 28:48.540
I did. Is that why you called me earlier?
Looking for validation?

28:48.541 --> 28:51.290
It's your fault that I'm needy.
Mom and Dad liked you best.

28:51.291 --> 28:53.540
Naturally.

28:53.541 --> 28:54.708
Hey, where are you?

28:55.291 --> 28:58.375
Uh, I'm at the, uh…

28:59.041 --> 29:00.625
the Briggs Motor Lodge.

29:01.625 --> 29:02.625
In Maine.

29:05.833 --> 29:06.666
Why?

29:11.375 --> 29:13.457
I needed to see David.

29:13.458 --> 29:15.249
Okay? And before you say anything,

29:15.250 --> 29:17.624
and I know I should've told you,
but I knew how you'd feel.

29:17.625 --> 29:18.957
Yet you did it anyway.

29:18.958 --> 29:22.374
Cheryl, can you please let me explain?
All right? I don't--

29:22.375 --> 29:25.415
Rachel, I don't care, okay?
Whatever it is, I don't care.

29:25.416 --> 29:27.249
Cheryl, listen. You need to hear this.

29:27.250 --> 29:29.083
No, Rachel. You need to hear me.

29:30.166 --> 29:32.333
I am done talking about this.

29:34.041 --> 29:35.207
I gotta go.

29:35.208 --> 29:36.375
I…

29:55.291 --> 29:56.625
Wake up, Burroughs.

30:09.458 --> 30:11.375
I need to take you to the infirmary.

30:13.250 --> 30:16.040
- What time is it?
- Time for you to do what I'm telling you.

30:16.041 --> 30:17.708
Let's go. Up.

30:26.250 --> 30:27.166
What's with the key?

30:27.875 --> 30:30.165
Want me to buzz it open,
wake all these monsters up?

30:30.166 --> 30:32.832
You know what kind of shit show
that would be?

30:32.833 --> 30:33.833
Come on, walk.

30:38.958 --> 30:40.416
What's going on?

30:41.000 --> 30:44.790
Ross Sumner filed a complaint.
Doctor needs to catalog your injuries.

30:44.791 --> 30:45.916
It won't take long.

30:49.625 --> 30:50.750
Go.

30:51.958 --> 30:53.125
Let's go.

31:16.041 --> 31:17.000
I'm sorry, Burroughs.

31:23.500 --> 31:25.041
Help!

31:29.000 --> 31:31.875
Someone! Help!

31:33.791 --> 31:35.291
Help me!

31:36.333 --> 31:38.958
Guard!

31:40.000 --> 31:41.291
Guards!

31:42.166 --> 31:45.957
Help! Please! Please don't do this!

31:45.958 --> 31:47.832
Help!

31:47.833 --> 31:48.750
Guards!

31:49.333 --> 31:50.707
Oh, shit.

31:50.708 --> 31:54.041
- It's over, Burroughs. It's over.
- Why are you trying to kill me?

31:55.250 --> 31:56.750
I don't have a choice.

31:57.416 --> 31:58.457
I took their money.

31:58.458 --> 32:00.291
Who… Whose money?

32:00.875 --> 32:02.457
Prisoner's loose!

32:02.458 --> 32:03.500
Oh!

32:19.458 --> 32:20.999
I knew you wouldn't let me down.

32:21.000 --> 32:23.665
- How you doing, kiddo?
- I'm hanging in there.

32:23.666 --> 32:26.332
I have to admit,
I was surprised by your call.

32:26.333 --> 32:28.041
Not disappointed, I hope.

32:28.833 --> 32:31.290
Did you have a chance
to look into Hilde Winslow for me?

32:31.291 --> 32:33.791
You know I did.
You want to tell me what this is about?

32:34.750 --> 32:35.874
I'm not sure yet. Why?

32:35.875 --> 32:39.582
Well, for one thing,
Hilde Winslow is no longer her legal name.

32:39.583 --> 32:41.625
It's now Harriet Winchester.

32:43.458 --> 32:46.541
- When did she change it?
- November 2021.

32:48.583 --> 32:52.666
That's a month after her testimony
sent my brother-in-law to prison.

32:54.291 --> 32:57.624
Someone doesn't usually change their name
unless they want to disappear.

32:57.625 --> 33:00.707
She sold her house in Revere
and pretty much dropped off the map.

33:00.708 --> 33:01.832
No current address?

33:01.833 --> 33:05.540
Only one I could find was a P.O. box
in New York under her new name.

33:05.541 --> 33:07.040
New York City?

33:07.041 --> 33:09.666
- She have friends or family there?
- None that I could find.

33:10.291 --> 33:12.290
Sounds like Hilde
doesn't want to be found.

33:12.291 --> 33:14.374
Sounds like someone's working a story.

33:14.375 --> 33:16.165
It's about time, Rachel.

33:16.166 --> 33:20.165
Now listen,
when you're ready to share, call me.

33:20.166 --> 33:22.000
Thanks. I'll be in touch.

33:31.041 --> 33:33.166
I had to give you a few stitches.

33:33.958 --> 33:36.249
You can have Advil or Tylenol,
whichever you prefer.

33:36.250 --> 33:39.500
There's no time, Doc.
We gotta take Mr. Burroughs to Ad Seg.

33:47.750 --> 33:49.583
You tried to kill
a corrections officer, Burroughs.

33:50.333 --> 33:51.250
Is that what he said?

33:52.291 --> 33:55.291
You ain't gonna survive the day.
I promise you.

33:59.041 --> 34:00.957
Officer Wesson. Officer Lu.

34:00.958 --> 34:03.374
- You okay?
- I got lucky.

34:03.375 --> 34:06.165
We were just about
to escort Mr. Burroughs to Ad Seg.

34:06.166 --> 34:08.000
- Warden.
- Save it. Save it.

34:08.791 --> 34:11.415
You and Sumner try to kill each other,
I don't give a shit.

34:11.416 --> 34:12.915
Law of the jungle keeps the peace.

34:12.916 --> 34:15.833
But go after my officers,
you're crossing an uncrossable line.

34:16.750 --> 34:17.999
Didn't go after anyone.

34:18.000 --> 34:19.999
Officer Wesson's report was pretty clear.

34:20.000 --> 34:21.290
You faked an illness.

34:21.291 --> 34:23.624
You demanded
to be brought to the infirmary.

34:23.625 --> 34:25.165
And then on the way here,
you attacked him.

34:25.166 --> 34:26.250
And you believe that?

34:27.291 --> 34:28.625
Do I believe

34:29.125 --> 34:32.916
the word of a decorated officer
over the word of a child killer?

34:33.500 --> 34:34.416
Yes.

34:35.708 --> 34:36.791
I do.

34:40.125 --> 34:41.540
I'm gonna take Mr. Burroughs

34:41.541 --> 34:44.332
and get him processed
for his new home in Ad Seg.

34:44.333 --> 34:46.415
You've had a long night, Ted.

34:46.416 --> 34:48.541
I want you to take
the rest of the day off.

34:50.000 --> 34:51.000
Yes, sir.

34:53.250 --> 34:54.083
Get him up.

35:12.083 --> 35:14.208
Philip, if I go to Ad Seg, I'm a dead man.

35:15.125 --> 35:16.750
You're not going to Ad Seg.

35:19.541 --> 35:21.249
Officer Diego called me after it happened.

35:21.250 --> 35:24.375
He told me he saw Wesson plant
a shiv on you after you got knocked out.

35:26.625 --> 35:29.083
Wesson said someone paid him to kill me.

35:31.583 --> 35:34.457
Well, I don't think
Ross Sumner was an accident either.

35:34.458 --> 35:36.082
Which means whoever wants you dead

35:36.083 --> 35:38.333
has the reach
to buy inmates and guards alike.

35:39.958 --> 35:43.041
And this all started after Rachel
showed you that photo of Matthew.

35:44.250 --> 35:46.083
- I told you.
- I know.

35:48.083 --> 35:49.250
I'm sorry.

35:50.166 --> 35:52.375
But you're gonna have
to trust me now, David.

35:52.875 --> 35:56.083
Because I can't protect you here anymore,
and I told your father I would.

36:08.125 --> 36:09.666
You look like shit.

36:23.583 --> 36:26.166
- What are you doing here?
- What, it's not obvious?

36:27.000 --> 36:28.166
We're here to break you out.

36:29.375 --> 36:32.124
What are you, crazy?
If you get caught, you'll lose everything.

36:32.125 --> 36:33.957
You'll die if you stay here.

36:33.958 --> 36:36.040
And we're not gonna let that happen.

36:36.041 --> 36:37.207
We don't have a lot of time.

36:37.208 --> 36:39.040
If this is gonna work,
we gotta take you through the plan.

36:39.041 --> 36:41.083
- Wait, we have a plan?
- We do.

36:42.208 --> 36:45.374
And if it all goes well,
you'll walk right out of here.

36:45.375 --> 36:48.707
Okay, there's one checkpoint
between my office and the elevator.

36:48.708 --> 36:51.874
It's a low-security crossover
used mainly by COs.

36:51.875 --> 36:53.915
Just keep your head down,
and we should be fine.

36:53.916 --> 36:54.957
Even with my head down,

36:54.958 --> 36:56.832
won't the guard
want to see a transfer order?

36:56.833 --> 36:59.165
No, because you won't
be wearing your prison jumpsuit.

36:59.166 --> 37:00.790
You'll be wearing Adam's uniform.

37:00.791 --> 37:02.124
Next, we'll move
through the visitors' exit,

37:02.125 --> 37:04.415
which leads right out
to the main parking lot.

37:04.416 --> 37:07.415
From there, you'll take Adam's cruiser
and have a two-hour head start

37:07.416 --> 37:09.541
before roll call even notices you're gone.

37:10.333 --> 37:12.707
Now remember what to do
if anybody finds you before I get back.

37:12.708 --> 37:17.207
David caught me off guard, took my gun,
put me in the closet, cuffed me.

37:17.208 --> 37:21.040
If not, everyone will assume Adam drove
off, and I'll sneak him out later tonight.

37:21.041 --> 37:22.541
Adam, I…

37:23.125 --> 37:27.041
You don't know what you'd do without me?
It's been that way since we were kids.

37:31.791 --> 37:33.416
Go find Matthew.

37:45.083 --> 37:47.374
Heard what happened with Burroughs.
You heading home?

37:47.375 --> 37:51.582
Yeah, yeah. At least that SOB
will enjoy a stretch in Ad Seg, right?

37:51.583 --> 37:54.583
What are you talking about?
I just came from Ad Seg.

37:55.166 --> 37:57.583
- The warden didn't drop him off?
- No.

38:41.875 --> 38:43.166
Excuse me, warden!

38:47.625 --> 38:50.207
Ted, I thought I told you to go home.

38:50.208 --> 38:54.249
I just spoke to the Ad Seg officer.
He said you never dropped off Burroughs.

38:54.250 --> 38:58.040
Yeah. I was gonna take him over
just after I walked my son out.

38:58.041 --> 38:59.208
Go home, Ted.

39:00.916 --> 39:01.958
Yes, sir.

39:11.333 --> 39:12.375
Burroughs?

39:18.791 --> 39:20.082
Hey, whoa! Let him go!

39:20.083 --> 39:22.833
- Step back or I will kill him!
- Do not do this, Burroughs!

39:24.208 --> 39:26.665
Goddamn it! Burroughs has taken
the warden hostage!

39:26.666 --> 39:31.790
Lock the prison down right now!
Lock it down! We got a hostage situation!

39:31.791 --> 39:33.874
Shit. Shit, it didn't work.
What are we gonna do?

39:33.875 --> 39:36.499
Okay, David, they're gonna
be waiting for us, okay?

39:36.500 --> 39:38.915
So you get behind me,
you put the gun on me,

39:38.916 --> 39:40.415
and you follow my lead, okay?

39:40.416 --> 39:42.125
You can do this. Come on!

39:47.041 --> 39:48.624
Put your gun down!

39:48.625 --> 39:51.415
Don't do this, Burroughs! On the ground!

39:51.416 --> 39:52.291
Lower your weapons!

39:53.208 --> 39:55.957
- Lower your weapons!
- Put the gun down now!

39:55.958 --> 39:58.749
- Put the gun down now!
- I said lower your weapons! Do it now!

39:58.750 --> 39:59.666
Do what he says!

40:00.666 --> 40:02.749
- Okay.
- Put 'em on the ground!

40:02.750 --> 40:04.874
- Keep going! Back off!
- Do it right now!

40:04.875 --> 40:07.333
- Buzz us through! Buzz us through!
- Hit the buzzer!

40:09.875 --> 40:12.332
- Hold on. Where's the cruiser?
- It's the visitors' lot. No time.

40:12.333 --> 40:14.750
- We'll take my truck. It's over here.
- Stand down!

40:15.916 --> 40:17.083
Stand down!

40:17.708 --> 40:21.041
Get back! Stay where you are!
Stay where you are!

40:43.041 --> 40:43.958
They're not moving.

40:46.500 --> 40:47.333
They're not moving!

40:48.458 --> 40:50.125
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!

40:52.875 --> 40:54.041
Hang on!

41:06.208 --> 41:08.540
Burroughs just escaped
in the warden's pickup.

41:08.541 --> 41:09.707
Alert the state police!

41:09.708 --> 41:12.707
Be advised,
male subject's last known location

41:12.708 --> 41:14.374
was south on Highway 1.

41:14.375 --> 41:16.291
Patrol cars in pursuit.

41:17.833 --> 41:20.207
All vehicles be on alert
for a Ford pickup.

41:20.208 --> 41:22.750
Inmate last seen
fleeing Briggs Penitentiary.

41:25.708 --> 41:28.875
Subject is armed and extremely dangerous.

41:29.833 --> 41:32.041
Go! They're gaining!

41:35.666 --> 41:39.124
We interrupt our regularly
scheduled program for breaking news.

41:39.125 --> 41:43.582
Reports are coming in of an escape out
of Briggs Maximum Security Penitentiary.

41:43.583 --> 41:48.207
Few details are in, but we can confirm
that the inmate's name is David Burroughs.

41:48.208 --> 41:52.415
Five years ago, Burroughs was convicted
for the brutal murder of his son Matthew,

41:52.416 --> 41:55.458
a case that made national headlines
and gripped the nation.

41:56.958 --> 41:59.000
All right, everyone, in position.

42:13.416 --> 42:14.915
- Now what?
- That depends.

42:14.916 --> 42:16.083
- On what?
- Them.

42:25.250 --> 42:28.332
Spike strip deployed.
We have the vehicle boxed in.

42:28.333 --> 42:29.625
They have nowhere to go.

42:32.500 --> 42:34.041
That'll be the negotiator.

42:34.750 --> 42:35.957
We're gonna negotiate?

42:35.958 --> 42:37.041
No, we're not.

42:37.583 --> 42:39.665
So you remember,
you're a desperate man. Okay?

42:39.666 --> 42:40.999
Whatever comes next, they need to believe

42:41.000 --> 42:43.250
that you'll do anything
not to go back, do you understand?

42:45.041 --> 42:48.707
Sniper now has a shot
and waiting for the go/no go.

42:48.708 --> 42:50.791
Yeah, that's not gonna be a problem.
